SUMMARY:Gevity: MVP feature sprint + green grid redesign + deploy spree
DESCRIPTION:Afternoon session on app-gevity-fit (Rails 8 fitness app) and t
 he gevity-fit marketing site. Implemented and shipped four MVP features\, 
 redesigned the consistency-grid color scheme across both repos\, then merg
 ed and production-deployed six PRs in sequence\, watching each deploy reso
 lve before moving to the next.\n\nDeliverables (merged + deployed):\n• #
 119 — Self-serve account deletion + data export\, retired the dead KillC
 ontroller (PR #130)\n• #133 — Green-only consistency grid palette\, dr
 op the light-cardio tile\, vertical split — app-gevity-fit (PR #134) and
  the gevity-fit marketing site\n• #109 — Cold-start fix (PR #127) — 
 confirmed live: /up response time went 22.5s to 0.14s\n• #125 — Automa
 ted pg_dump backups to Tigris (PR #126)\; nightly job still needs a one-ti
 me manual Tigris/Fly-secrets setup\n• #76 — Lifecycle jobs for the pre
 -loaded onboarding chart (PR #129) — required rebasing to resolve a conf
 ig/recurring.yml conflict against #125\n• #135 — Cardio dropdown: orde
 r by most-recent-use\, not frequency (filed + PR #136)\n\nOpened\, held fo
 r Trey's own review (not merged this session):\n• #30 — MFA via email 
 OTP (PR #131)\n• #32 — Slipping-schedule nudges (PR #132)\n\nAlso: rec
 overed an orphaned local git commit (8 historical ICS worklog files) via r
 eflog after an accidental git reset --hard.\n\nRaw (un-rounded) window: ~1
 3:00 EDT (research/implementation before the first commit at 13:50:17) to 
 15:32:11 EDT (#136 deploy completion). Rounded to 13:00-15:45.
